{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## SCANNER ROOT CAUSE FOUND -- three faults, and the third was new to everyone\n\nRead-only diagnosis dispatched (no claim, no edits, no CI cost) because with 17 changes frozen and\nthe cause unknown, INFORMATION was the bottleneck, not another workaround. Posted to 90c7.\n\nFAULT 1 (known): old-base patchsets lack scripts/install_review_scanners.py. The Verified lane\nresolves the WORKFLOW from trusted main but checks out the PATCHSET, so make/scripts come from the\npatchset.\n\nFAULT 2: 'set -euo pipefail' at the top of the scanner-integration make recipe. GNU make runs recipes\nunder /bin/sh = dash on ubuntu-latest. Measured ON MAIN (job 100919632441):\n  /bin/sh: 1: set: Illegal option -o pipefail\n  make: *** [Makefile:475: scanner-integration] Error 2\nvalidate-locks PASSES first -- the failure is the recipe's FIRST LINE, which is why it dies in\n30-50s. Already fixed by 6b034b9f8224.\n\nFAULT 3, NEW: with fault 2 fixed the job gets further and fails differently (job 100935522585):\n  Successfully installed ... semgrep-1.145.0\n  ERROR: could not execute .tools/review-scanners/bin/semgrep: [Errno 2] No such file or directory\nMakefile:503 passes a RELATIVE '--prefix .tools/review-scanners' while DEFAULT_PREFIX\n(install_review_scanners.py:22) is absolute. _link_semgrep (:335) does link.symlink_to(semgrep) with\na relative target, resolved relative to the SYMLINK'S OWN DIRECTORY, so it dangles. Gitleaks is fine\nbecause it uses shutil.copy2, not a symlink. Reproduced in a throwaway tmpdir with a byte-identical\nerror shape.\n\nIT CORRECTS THE REVERT'S PREMISE, which matters for whatever lands next: commit 9c7d78127696 claims\n'the pytest contract step fails on every change'. PYTEST NEVER RAN -- execution died in the install\nstep's own version check (Makefile:503), before check (504) and before pytest (506). The nine\ncontracts are UNTESTED, not failing. Nobody yet knows whether they pass.\n\nWHY IT ESCAPED LOCAL TESTING: a bare 'install' with no --prefix uses the absolute default and works.\nOnly the Makefile path is broken. So 'it works on my machine' was true and useless.\n\nThe skipped-vs-failure split I flagged earlier as possibly meaningful is NOT a clue: it is the\nschedule guard at test.yml:77-79, which also skips mutation on schedule runs. Good to have that ruled\nout rather than left as an open thread. And both items 2595's LLM review flagged are stale --\n_selected_prefix IS applied on both paths and --semgrep-venv IS read; CI passes neither flag.\n\nSUGGESTED FIX (not implemented, theirs to apply): resolve the prefix once at the boundary --\n_selected_prefix (:376) returns .resolve() -- rather than patching only symlink_to(semgrep.resolve()),\nbecause the relative-prefix hazard is latent at EVERY override call site. Plus a regression test\ninvoking the installer with a relative --prefix from a different cwd; existing tests only exercise\nthe absolute default.\n\nI am not implementing it. 90c7 is another session's and I told the operator I would want say-so\nbefore touching their work. Diagnosis is information contribution and cannot conflict; a fix would.\nThe distinction held up well here -- the finding is worth more than a third rejected workaround."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788516079311177001,"uuid":"85cfea73-587d-495a-9046-287c5c0c3f5e"}